   "source": [
    "# Enter Machine Learning: A Paradigm Shift\n",
    "\n",
    "## The Core Insight\n",
    "\n",
    "What if we could **learn** the physics of electromagnetic devices from data, rather than solving Maxwell's equations from scratch every time?\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the promise of **statistical learning** applied to electromagnetic design.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Traditional Approach vs. ML Approach\n",
    "\n",
    "```mermaid\n",
    "graph LR\n",
    "    subgraph Traditional\n",
    "        A[Design Parameters] --> B[Maxwell's Equations]\n",
    "        B --> C[FEA Solver]\n",
    "        C --> D[Performance Results]\n",
    "    end\n",
    "    \n",
    "    subgraph Machine Learning\n",
    "        E[Design Parameters] --> F[Neural Network]\n",
    "        F --> G[Performance Results]\n",
    "        G --> H[Optional FEA Verification]\n",
    "    end\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Workflow\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Generate training data**: Run FEA on a representative sample of designs (thousands)\n",
    "2. **Train surrogate models**: Use deep learning to learn input-output mappings\n",
    "3. **Fast inference**: Predict performance for new designs in milliseconds\n",
    "4. **Massive speedup**: Explore millions of designs in the time FEA handles hundreds"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Let's quantify the speedup potential\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Time comparison\n",
    "fea_time_per_design = 2  # hours for 2D FEA\n",
    "ml_inference_time = 0.02  # seconds for neural network prediction\n",
    "\n",
    "# Speedup calculation\n",
    "speedup_factor = (fea_time_per_design * 3600) / ml_inference_time\n",
    "print(f\"FEA time per design: {fea_time_per_design} hours\")\n",
    "print(f\"ML inference time: {ml_inference_time} seconds\")\n",
    "print(f\"Speedup factor: {speedup_factor:,.0f}×\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Design exploration comparison\n",
    "designs_per_week_fea = 7 * 24 / fea_time_per_design  # Running FEA continuously\n",
    "designs_per_week_ml = 7 * 24 * 3600 / ml_inference_time  # Running ML predictions continuously\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nDesigns per week:\")\n",
    "print(f\"FEA: {designs_per_week_fea:.0f} designs\")\n",
    "print(f\"ML: {designs_per_week_ml:,.0f} designs\")\n",
    "print(f\"Exploration increase: {designs_per_week_ml/designs_per_week_fea:,.0f}×\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Three Key Advantages\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Speed: Dramatic Acceleration\n",
    "\n",
    "The most obvious advantage is computational speed:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **FEA**: 1 hour per geometry\n",
    "- **Neural network**: 0.02 seconds per geometry\n",
    "- **Speedup**: 180,000×\n",
    "\n",
    "This transforms what's possible in design exploration."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize the speed impact\n",
    "fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(15, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Time for different numbers of designs\n",
    "num_designs = [10, 100, 1000, 10000, 100000]\n",
    "fea_times = [n * fea_time_per_design for n in num_designs]  # hours\n",
    "ml_times = [n * ml_inference_time / 3600 for n in num_designs]  # hours\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 1: Linear scale\n",
    "ax1.plot(num_designs, fea_times, 'b-o', label='FEA', linewidth=2, markersize=8)\n",
    "ax1.plot(num_designs, ml_times, 'r-o', label='ML', linewidth=2, markersize=8)\n",
    "ax1.set_xlabel('Number of Designs')\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel('Time (hours)')\n",
    "ax1.set_title('Computation Time Comparison (Linear Scale)')\n",
    "ax1.legend()\n",
    "ax1.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "ax1.set_yscale('log')\n",
    "ax1.set_xscale('log')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 2: What becomes feasible\n",
    "scenarios = ['Current practice', 'Aggressive optimization', 'ML-enabled exploration']\n",
    "designs_feasible = [100, 1000, 1000000]\n",
    "colors = ['red', 'orange', 'green']\n",
    "\n",
    "bars = ax2.bar(scenarios, designs_feasible, color=colors, alpha=0.7)\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel('Number of Designs Evaluated')\n",
    "ax2.set_title('Design Space Exploration Capacity')\n",
    "ax2.set_yscale('log')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add value labels on bars\n",
    "for bar, value in zip(bars, designs_feasible):\n",
    "    height = bar.get_height()\n",
    "    ax2.text(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2., height,\n",
    "             f'{value:,.0f}', ha='center', va='bottom', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate what becomes practical\n",
    "print(\"What becomes practical with ML:\")\n",
    "print(f\"- Current practice (~100 designs): {100 * fea_time_per_design} hours = {100 * fea_time_per_design / 24:.1f} days\")\n",
    "print(f\"- With ML (~1M designs): {1000000 * ml_inference_time / 3600:.1f} hours\")\n",
    "print(f\"- Time saved: {(100 * fea_time_per_design) - (1000000 * ml_inference_time / 3600):.1f} hours\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2. Parallelizability: GPU Acceleration\n",
    "\n",
    "Machine learning predictions can be massively parallelized:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Batch predictions**: Evaluate 1000 designs simultaneously\n",
    "- **GPU acceleration**: Graphics cards optimized for matrix operations\n",
    "- **Cloud scaling**: Distribute across multiple machines if needed\n",
    "\n",
    "Compare this to FEA, which typically processes designs sequentially with limited parallelization."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Demonstrate batch processing advantage\n",
    "import time\n",
    "\n",
    "# Simulate sequential vs batch processing\n",
    "num_designs = 1000\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sequential processing (like FEA)\n",
    "sequential_time = num_designs * fea_time_per_design  # hours\n",
    "\n",
    "# Batch processing (like ML on GPU)\n",
    "batch_size = 1000  # GPU can handle this many at once\n",
    "batch_time = (num_designs / batch_size) * (ml_inference_time / 3600)  # hours\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Processing {num_designs:,} designs:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Sequential (FEA-like): {sequential_time:.1f} hours ({sequential_time/24:.1f} days)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Batch (ML-like): {batch_time:.4f} hours ({batch_time*60:.2f} minutes)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Batch speedup: {sequential_time/batch_time:,.0f}×\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visualize scaling\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "design_counts = [100, 500, 1000, 5000, 10000]\n",
    "sequential_times = [n * fea_time_per_design for n in design_counts]\n",
    "batch_times = [(n / batch_size) * (ml_inference_time / 3600) for n in design_counts]\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.loglog(design_counts, sequential_times, 'b-o', label='Sequential (FEA)', linewidth=2)\n",
    "ax.loglog(design_counts, batch_times, 'r-o', label='Batch (ML)', linewidth=2)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Number of Designs')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Processing Time (hours)')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Sequential vs Batch Processing Scaling')\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3. Enables Advanced Workflows\n",
    "\n",
    "The speed and parallelizability of ML enable entirely new design workflows:\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Design Optimization\n",
    "- **Gradient-based optimization**: Run thousands of evaluations per iteration\n",
    "- **Genetic algorithms**: Large populations with many generations\n",
    "- **Multi-objective optimization**: Explore Pareto fronts comprehensively\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Real-time Interaction\n",
    "- **Interactive design tools**: Designers explore design spaces in real-time\n",
    "- **Parametric studies**: Instant feedback as parameters change\n",
    "- **Sensitivity analysis**: Quick identification of critical parameters\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Uncertainty Quantification\n",
    "- **Monte Carlo analysis**: Thousands of samples for statistical confidence\n",
    "- **Robust design optimization**: Account for manufacturing variations\n",
    "- **Reliability assessment**: Probability of meeting specifications"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example: Genetic algorithm comparison\n",
    "population_size = 100\n",
    "num_generations = 100\n",
    "total_evaluations = population_size * num_generations\n",
    "\n",
    "ga_time_fea = total_evaluations * fea_time_per_design  # hours\n",
    "ga_time_ml = total_evaluations * ml_inference_time / 3600  # hours\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Genetic Algorithm Comparison:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Population size: {population_size}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Generations: {num_generations}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total evaluations: {total_evaluations:,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"FEA time: {ga_time_fea:.1f} hours ({ga_time_fea/24:.1f} days)\")\n",
    "print(f\"ML time: {ga_time_ml:.3f} hours ({ga_time_ml*60:.1f} minutes)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Time reduction: {ga_time_fea/ga_time_ml:,.0f}×\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# What becomes feasible\n",
    "feasible_generations_fea = (24 * 7) / (population_size * fea_time_per_design)  # One week\n",
    "feasible_generations_ml = (24 * 7) / (population_size * ml_inference_time / 3600)  # One week\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nGenerations possible in one week:\")\n",
    "print(f\"With FEA: {feasible_generations_fea:.1f} generations\")\n",
    "print(f\"With ML: {feasible_generations_ml:.0f} generations\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## The Trade-off\n",
    "\n",
    "Machine learning models are **surrogates**, not replacements for physics simulations:\n",
    "\n",
    "### Accuracy Considerations\n",
    "- **Typical error**: 0.1-1% compared to FEA reference\n",
    "- **Training dependency**: Quality depends on training data coverage\n",
    - **Generalization limits**: Performance degrades outside training distribution\n",
    "\n",
    "### Verification Strategy\n",
    "The most effective approach is **hybrid**:\n",
    "1. **ML for exploration**: Rapidly evaluate thousands of designs\n",
    "2. **Identify promising candidates**: Select top 0.1% of designs\n",
    "3. **FEA verification**: Verify promising designs with high-fidelity simulation\n",
    "4. **Iterate refinement**: Add new FEA results to training data if needed\n",
    "\n",
    "This combines the **speed of ML** with the **accuracy of FEA**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Hybrid workflow efficiency calculation\n",
    "total_designs_explored = 1000000  # ML explores 1M designs\n",
    "top_percentage = 0.001  # Top 0.1% selected for FEA\n",
    "fea_verifications = int(total_designs_explored * top_percentage / 100)\n",
    "\n",
    "ml_exploration_time = total_designs_explored * ml_inference_time / 3600  # hours\n",
    "fea_verification_time = fea_verifications * fea_time_per_design  # hours\n",
    "total_hybrid_time = ml_exploration_time + fea_verification_time\n",
    "\n",
    "traditional_designs = 100  # What designers typically evaluate\n",
    "traditional_time = traditional_designs * fea_time_per_design  # hours\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Hybrid Workflow Analysis:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Designs explored with ML: {total_designs_explored:,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Designs verified with FEA: {fea_verifications:,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"ML exploration time: {ml_exploration_time:.2f} hours\")\n",
    "print(f\"FEA verification time: {fea_verification_time:.1f} hours\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total hybrid time: {total_hybrid_time:.1f} hours\")\n",
    "print(f\"Traditional approach time: {traditional_time:.1f} hours\")\n",
    "print(f\"Design space exploration increase: {total_designs_explored/traditional_designs:,.0f}×\")\n",
    "print(f\"Time efficiency: {traditional_time/total_hybrid_time:.1f}×\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Key Takeaways\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Massive speedup**: 180,000× faster predictions enable unprecedented design exploration\n",
    "2. **Parallel processing**: GPU acceleration makes batch evaluation extremely efficient\n",
    "3. **New workflows**: Enables optimization strategies that were previously impractical\n",
    "4. **Hybrid approach**: Combine ML speed with FEA accuracy for best results\n",
    "\n",
    "Machine learning doesn't replace physics simulation—it **augments** it, making it possible to explore design spaces that were previously inaccessible.\n",
    "\n",
    "In the next sections, we'll explore the specific machine learning techniques that make this transformation possible."
   ]
